WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.950
[Soft original electronic score]

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.489
After dark, a signal finds its people.

00:00:05.339 --> 00:00:11.322
In east London, rave spaces and pirate radio helped new sounds find their audiences.

00:00:12.172 --> 00:00:20.210
The early nineteen nineties connected local music spaces with experiments in hardcore, jungle, and drum and bass.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:30.098
This contemporary illustrated essay traces the idea of those connections. The score is original, not a historical broadcast.

